I have created a typed mock API layer for the Yabhasyuka website that perfectly matches the requested contract and compiles cleanly under strict TypeScript. I defined all the custom TypeScript interfaces in `src/lib/api/types.ts`, set up comprehensive mock data matching the quiet luxury and soft wellness brand voice across the files in `src/lib/data/`, and implemented the corresponding asynchronous endpoints in `src/lib/api/index.ts`. The API mock includes simulated latency (~300ms), a deterministic 70% available slot generator utilizing a polynomial hash paired with a linear congruential generator, strict input validations (email format, WhatsApp length, required fields), and a stable, deterministic booking reference generator formatting codes as `YBS-XXXXXX`.
